# Six functions are ever handed in, and each takes and returns a number in a register. A call by value would box the number, the entry of the callee would take it out of its box, and so again for the result:
# the word of the closure is loaded once and compared five times, and each arm is a direct call with the double in its register on the way in and on the way out.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="apply" role=Source
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[word]] = Load(b@[[operation]], offset = 12, ControlDependent|Reads:AOTSlimClosure_word,
# CHECK-COUNT-5: = Equal(b@[[word]],
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# CALLS-LABEL: name="apply" role=Source
# CALLS-COUNT-6: Double b@{{*}} = Patchpoint(b@{{*}}:Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = Register({{*}}), ControlDependent, {{*}}:CallDirect)
# CALLS-LABEL: end of function
# The word is loaded once. Nothing is boxed, nothing that comes back is tested or converted.
# NONE-LABEL: name="apply" role=Source
# NONE-NOT: pureFunction
# NONE-NOT: IToD(
# NONE-NOT: BitwiseCast(
# NONE-NOT: AboveEqual(
# NONE-LABEL: end of function
# X64: instructions: 17, patchpoints: 6, rare instructions: 1
# ARM64: instructions: 23, patchpoints: 6, rare instructions: 1
